{"document_id": "20cd3e38-5222-49fd-b25e-28d3b03a189a", "crop": "mango", "organization": "Unknown", "source": "Unknown", "source_url": "https://mango-crop.web.app/diseasemanage/dismgtblosumblight1.htm", "title": "Mango - Solutions for crop management", "retrieved_at": "2026-09-07T00:13:40.655755", "content": "  * [Skip navigation](https://mango-crop.web.app/diseasemanage/dismgtblosumblight1.htm#content)\n  * [Home](https://mango-crop.web.app/)\n\n\n# ![](https://mango-crop.web.app/diseasemanage/imgs/dismgtpmhdr.jpg)\n[Home](https://mango-crop.web.app/) > [Previous Page](https://mango-crop.web.app/diseasemanage/dismgtblosumblight1.htm#) > Current\n##  Disease management module**:: Fungal- Blossom blight**\n### Bacterial & Other Diseases\n**Bacterial Diseases** : They can cause a variety of symptoms including cankers, leaf spots, overgrowths, scabs, wilts, and others\n  * ![cancker](https://mango-crop.web.app/diseasemanage/anthra1/cankerleavess.jpg)\n  * ![Other](https://mango-crop.web.app/diseasemanage/anthra1/redrust1s.jpg)\n\n\n**Others:** This disease attack can causes reduction in photosynthetic activity and defoliation of leaves thereby reducing the vitality of the host plant.\n###  Fungal Diseases -  Blossom blight \n**Associated pathogens:**\n_**C. gloeosporiodes**_\n_**Alternaria alternata**_\n**_Pestaliopsis mangiferae_**\n####  Blossom blight at various parts of mango\nMove mouse over the image to view more details:\n  * [ ![Blossom blight \\(thumbnail\\)](https://mango-crop.web.app/diseasemanage/anthra1/blosumblight1s.jpg)](https://mango-crop.web.app/diseasemanage/anthra1/blosumblight1.jpg)![ Disease \\(larger image\\)](https://mango-crop.web.app/diseasemanage/anthra1/blosumblight1.jpg) Symptoms and control !   \n**Blossom blight :****Panicles are infected by Blossom blight, Infected panicles are shown in picture, panicles do not develope further.**\n  * [ ![Blossom blight\\(thumbnail\\)](https://mango-crop.web.app/diseasemanage/anthra1/blosumblight2s.jpg)](https://mango-crop.web.app/diseasemanage/anthra1/blosumblight2.jpg)![ Disease \\(larger image\\)](https://mango-crop.web.app/diseasemanage/anthra1/blosumblight2.jpg) Symptoms and control !   \n**Blossom blight :** **Panicles do not develop fully and result in heavy crop loss**.\n\n\n  * [ ![Blossom blight \\(thumbnail\\)](https://mango-crop.web.app/diseasemanage/anthra1/blossomblight3s.jpg)](https://mango-crop.web.app/diseasemanage/anthra1/blossomblight3.jpg)![ Disease \\(larger image\\)](https://mango-crop.web.app/diseasemanage/anthra1/blossomblight3.jpg) Symptoms and control !   \n**Blossom blight :Black spots on foliage that withers, Blossom is blighted beginning from bud swelling**\n  * [ ![Blossum blight \\(thumbnail\\)](https://mango-crop.web.app/diseasemanage/anthra1/blossomblight4s.jpg)](https://mango-crop.web.app/diseasemanage/anthra1/blossomblight4.jpg)![ Disease \\(larger image\\)](https://mango-crop.web.app/diseasemanage/anthra1/blossomblight4.jpg) Symptoms and control !   \n**Blossom blight :Panicle are not develop fully Heavy crop loss or total destruction**\n\n\n  * [ ![Blossom blight \\(thumbnail\\)](https://mango-crop.web.app/diseasemanage/anthra1/blosumblight5s.jpg)](https://mango-crop.web.app/diseasemanage/anthra1/blosumblight5.jpg)![ Disease \\(larger image\\)](https://mango-crop.web.app/diseasemanage/anthra1/blosumblight5.jpg) Symptoms and control !   \n**Blossom blight :** : **The blossom appear blighted from the bud swelling stage and whole blossom turn into the black thick mass of the tissue**\n  * [ ![Blossum blight \\(thumbnail\\)](https://mango-crop.web.app/diseasemanage/anthra1/blosumblight6s.jpg)](https://mango-crop.web.app/diseasemanage/anthra1/blosumblight6.jpg)![ Disease \\(larger image\\)](https://mango-crop.web.app/diseasemanage/anthra1/blosumblight6.jpg) Symptoms and control !   \n**Blossom blight :** **Tree affected by Blossom blight. This disease causes heavy damage to the panicles**\n\n\n( Move mouse over a thumbnail for a full sized version)\n**Blossom blight :** This disease causes heavy damage to the panicles. The blossom appear blighted from the bud swelling stage and whole blossom turn into the black thick mass of the tissue. Panicles do not develop fully and result in heavy crop loss. \n  * [Home ](https://mango-crop.web.app/index.html)\n  * [Technologies](https://mango-crop.web.app/Technologies.html)\n  * [Varieties ](https://mango-crop.web.app/var/varieties.html)\n  * [Crop production](https://mango-crop.web.app/diseasemanage/dismgtblosumblight1.htm#)\n  * [Crop Protection](https://mango-crop.web.app/cropprotect.html)\n  * [Crop improvement](https://mango-crop.web.app/cropimprove.html)\n  * [Machineries](https://mango-crop.web.app/Technologies/machineries.html)\n  * [Contact us](https://mango-crop.web.app/ContactUs.html)\n  * Pest management\n\n\nMango crop managemnt and Diagnostic system::Developed by MK CHANDRA PRAKASH & REENA ROSY THOMAS\n", "html": "<!DOCTYPE html><html lang=\"en\"><head>\n<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n<title>Mango - Solutions for crop management</title>\n<meta name=\"description\" content=\"enter a brief description of your website here\">\n<meta name=\"keywords\" content=\"enter, some, keywords, seperated by, commas\">\n\n<!--STYLESHEETS-->\n<link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"assets/style.css\" type=\"text/css\" media=\"screen\">\n<link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"assets/print.css\" type=\"text/css\" media=\"print\">\n<!--INTERNET EXPLORER SPECIFIC STYLESHEETS-->\n<!--[if lte IE 8]>\n<link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"assets/ie8_hacks.css\" type=\"text/css\" media=\"screen\" />\n<![endif]-->\n\n<!--Hekp IE8 and earlier with HTML5-->\n<!--[if lt IE 9]>\n<script src=\"http://html5shiv.googlecode.com/svn/trunk/html5.js\"></script>\n<![endif]-->\n\n<!--GOOGLE WEB FONTS USED IN THIS TEMPLATE - http://www.google.com/webfonts-->\n<link href=\"http://fonts.googleapis.com/css?family=Happy+Monkey\" rel=\"stylesheet\" type=\"text/css\">\n<style type=\"text/css\">\n.auto-style1 {\